          "y" : 171
        },
        {
          "height" : 9.2,
          "text" : "bench@paper-model.example",
          "width" : 130.8,
          "x" : 320.6,
          "y" : 183.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "Abstract",
          "width" : 44.5,
          "x" : 283.8,
          "y" : 221.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "A folded card spacer fixes the height of a model rail above its baseboard. We",
          "width" : 324.3,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 246.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "measured spacers folded from three card stocks in a single test slot and",
          "width" : 324.3,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 257.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "compared the measured heights with a simple layer model. The model predicts",
          "width" : 324.3,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 268.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "the height of a folded spacer to within a tenth of a millimetre when the crease",
          "width" : 324.3,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 279.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "allowance is taken from a two-layer trial. We describe the slot, the measurement",
          "width" : 324.3,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 290.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "procedure and the remaining sources of error, and we list practical rules for",
          "width" : 324.3,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 301.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "choosing a card stock for a given rail height.",
          "width" : 177.3,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 312.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "1 Introduction",
          "width" : 82.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 344.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Paper models of railways need many small parts of exact height. Rails, platform edges and signal",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 369
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "bases all sit on spacers, and a spacer that is too thick by a fraction of a millimetre lifts a rail joint",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 379.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "enough to derail a light wagon. Most builders cut spacers from card and fold them until they reach",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 390.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "the height they want (Model Rail Desk, 2025). Folding is quick and needs no tools, but the height",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 401.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "of a folded spacer is not simply the sum of the card thicknesses: each crease adds a small allowance,",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 412.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "and the allowance depends on the card and on how firmly the crease is pressed.",
          "width" : 316.2,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 423.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "This note reports a bench trial of folded spacers. Our aims were:",
          "width" : 256.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 439.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "•",
          "width" : 3.5,
          "x" : 135.4,
          "y" : 460.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "to measure the height of spacers with two to six layers in one fixed slot;",
          "width" : 286.1,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 460.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "•",
          "width" : 3.5,
          "x" : 135.4,
          "y" : 475.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "to compare the measurements with a layer model that adds a crease allowance; and",
          "width" : 330.6,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 475.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "•",
          "width" : 3.5,
          "x" : 135.4,
          "y" : 490.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "to give simple rules for choosing a card stock for a target height.",
          "width" : 256.8,
          "x" : 143.9,
          "y" : 490.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Section 2 describes the slot and the procedure, Section 3 reports the measurements, and Section 4",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 510.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "summarises the rules. Earlier notes on layered card (Card Stock Bench and Model Rail Desk, 2024)",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 521.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 12,
          "text" : "and on gauge blocks (Scale Fixture Room, 2023) motivated the layer model used here.1",
          "width" : 348.5,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 531.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "2 Method",
          "width" : 57.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 559.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "2.1 The test slot",
          "width" : 73.9,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 584.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "The slot was cut into a block of laminated board and lined with a strip of thin brass so that the card",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 604.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "could not dent the walls. A sliding rail of known height rests on top of the spacer, and the height is",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 615.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "read from a scale on the side of the block. The block was clamped to the bench throughout the trial",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 626.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "so that the scale did not move between readings.",
          "width" : 192.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 637.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Each spacer was inserted with its folded edge towards the back of the slot. The rail was lowered onto",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 653.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "it and left for ten seconds before the reading was taken, because a freshly folded spacer springs back",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 664.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "slowly. Three readings were taken for each spacer, removing and reinserting it between readings.",
          "width" : 386.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 675.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 6.6,
          "text" : "1",
          "width" : 3,
          "x" : 119.4,
          "y" : 694.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 8.8,
          "text" : "All parts were cut from the same sheets on the same afternoon, so the moisture content of the card was the same for",
          "width" : 381.6,
          "x" : 122.3,
          "y" : 695.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 8.8,
          "text" : "every spacer.",
          "width" : 41.6,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 705.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 8.8,
          "text" : "40th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems (NeurIPS 2026).",
          "width" : 246.4,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 732.7
        }
      ],
