        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Thick 4 1.98 1.92",
          "width" : 173.6,
          "x" : 219.2,
          "y" : 260.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "2.2 Layer model",
          "width" : 76.2,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 293.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "We model the height h of a spacer with n layers of card of thickness t as",
          "width" : 288.9,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 313.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.7,
          "text" : "h= n t + (n− 1) c,",
          "width" : 82.1,
          "x" : 265,
          "y" : 329.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.7,
          "text" : "(1)",
          "width" : 11.6,
          "x" : 492.4,
          "y" : 329.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "where c is the crease allowance added by each fold. The allowance is found from a two-layer trial,",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 344.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 12.4,
          "text" : "for which Equation (1) gives c = h2− 2t. The same model was used for the gauge block of Scale",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 355.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Fixture Room (2023), where it predicted the height of folded board well for up to four layers.",
          "width" : 371.8,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 367.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "Card thickness.",
          "width" : 67.6,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 390.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11.1,
          "text" : "The thickness t was measured with a dial gauge on ten single sheets of each",
          "width" : 318.5,
          "x" : 185.5,
          "y" : 390.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "stock, and the mean was used in the model. The thin stock measured 0.20 mm, the medium stock",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 401.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "0.30 mm and the thick stock 0.45 mm, with a spread of less than 0.01 mm in every case.",
          "width" : 349.2,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 412.6
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Pressing the crease.",
          "width" : 84.4,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 435.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Every crease was pressed once with the flat of a bone folder along a steel",
          "width" : 301.7,
          "x" : 202.3,
          "y" : 435.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "rule. Pressing twice made the crease allowance smaller but also cracked the surface of the thick",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 447.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "stock, so a single pass was used for all spacers.",
          "width" : 187.3,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 458.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "3 Results",
          "width" : 55.1,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 483.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Figure 1 shows the slot with a four-layer spacer in place, and Table 1 lists the mean measured height",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 507.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "of each spacer together with the height predicted by Equation (1).",
          "width" : 261.4,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 518.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "The model agrees with the measurements to within 0.06 mm for every spacer. The largest error is for",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 535.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "the thick stock, where the crease allowance grows with the number of layers: the outer layers must",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 546
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "bend around a thicker core, and the crease opens slightly. For the thin and medium stocks the error",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 556.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "does not grow with the number of layers, which agrees with the note of Glue Pot Corner (2022) on",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 567.8
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "thin paper joints.",
          "width" : 67.2,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 578.7
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Repeated readings of the same spacer differed by at most 0.02 mm. Spacers that were left in the slot",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 595.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "overnight lost about 0.01 mm of height, which is smaller than the spread between readings and was",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 606
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "ignored.",
          "width" : 32.9,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 616.9
        },
        {
          "height" : 13.2,
          "text" : "4 Conclusion",
          "width" : 75.1,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 643.1
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "A folded card spacer can be designed from the card thickness and a crease allowance measured once",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 667.5
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "for each stock. For heights up to 2 mm the thin and medium stocks follow the layer model closely,",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 678.4
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "and they are the better choice when a rail must sit at an exact height. The thick stock is quicker to",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 689.3
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "fold but should be checked in the slot when more than three layers are used. A card ladder (Window",
          "width" : 396,
          "x" : 108,
          "y" : 700.2
        },
        {
          "height" : 11,
          "text" : "Frame Study, 2021) gives a convenient way to check many spacers at once.",
          "width" : 300.3,
